  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025-2026 CC Southern Africa Compounded Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people to be assisted: 15,000 individuals (3,000 households)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Chronic Crisis project aims to transition from emergency assistance to long-term resilience-building, ensuring that socio-economically vulnerable households can withstand future crises. The focus is to address immediate needs through the provision of humanitarian assistance, including safety nets, water solu&#x10019f;ons, and safeguarding measures for at-risk groups</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe is facing a severe crisis due to the 2023-2024 El Ni&#xf1;o-induced drought and mid-season dry spells, resulting in widespread water scarcity and crop failure. The country experienced one of the driest seasons in decades, leading to significant agricultural losses and food shortage</narrative>
  </description>
